# standard.buffer.semsig — generated signature sidecar (README §10.6, §29 #14).
# DEFERRED runtime (WS1-119): bounds-checked buffers/slices. A `Buffer` carries
# its length; element access is `buffer.get index` -> Result (byte or
# BufferBoundsError) — there is NO indexing/offset syntax in app source, so an
# out-of-bounds access is a checked error, never UB. `buffer.slice` returns a
# `Slice` that *borrows* the buffer (a WS1-111 view with the buffer's lifetime).

bufferSig is semsig
bufferSig version "1.0"
bufferSig generatedBy "eavc 0.1"
bufferSig describes standard.buffer

Buffer is alias
Buffer for OpaquePointer
Buffer purpose "A length-carrying byte buffer; element access is bounds-checked"

Slice is alias
Slice for OpaquePointer
Slice purpose "A non-owning view into a Buffer (borrows it, with the buffer's lifetime)"

ByteCount is alias
ByteCount for Int64
ByteCount purpose "A length / index measured in bytes"

BufferBoundsError is error
BufferBoundsError purpose "An index or range outside a buffer's length (never UB)"

bufferLength is intrinsic
bufferLength target buffer.length
bufferLength arg buffer Buffer
bufferLength out length ByteCount
bufferLength purpose "The buffer's length in bytes (deferred runtime)"

bufferGet is intrinsic
bufferGet target buffer.get
bufferGet arg buffer Buffer
bufferGet arg index ByteCount
bufferGet out value Byte
bufferGet catch BufferBoundsError
bufferGet purpose "Read one byte by index; out-of-bounds is a BufferBoundsError, never UB (deferred runtime)"

bufferSet is intrinsic
bufferSet target buffer.set
bufferSet arg buffer Buffer
bufferSet arg index ByteCount
bufferSet arg value Byte
bufferSet out written Int32
bufferSet catch BufferBoundsError
bufferSet purpose "Write one byte by index; out-of-bounds is a BufferBoundsError (deferred runtime)"

bufferSlice is intrinsic
bufferSlice target buffer.slice
bufferSlice arg buffer Buffer
bufferSlice arg start ByteCount
bufferSlice arg length ByteCount
bufferSlice out window Slice
bufferSlice catch BufferBoundsError
bufferSlice borrows buffer
bufferSlice lifetime buffer
bufferSlice mayEscape no
bufferSlice purpose "A bounds-checked sub-view that borrows the buffer (a non-owning Slice; deferred runtime)"
